      "id": "hv-0",
      "conflict": "Formal mathematical verification versus iterative resilience-based deployment",
      "prevails": "undecidable",
      "criterion": "scope",
      "rationale": "Neither side provides empirical data on the failure rates of large-scale neural networks under their preferred safety framework. Safetyist correctly identifies the risks of non-linear state-drift, while Accelerationist correctly notes that modularity can mitigate system-wide collapse.",
      "whatWouldChange": "Peer-reviewed studies comparing the catastrophic failure rates of monolithic vs. modular AI architectures during stress testing.",
