    },
    {
      "id": "hv-1",
      "conflict": "Mandatory red-teaming as an innovation tax versus a public safety dividend",
      "prevails": "C2",
      "criterion": "logical_validity",
      "rationale": "Skeptic successfully reframes the debate by identifying the externalization of risk, which standard economic theory recognizes as a market failure. Accelerationist treats innovation as an intrinsic good without accounting for the negative externalities that typically justify government intervention in high-risk sectors.",
      "whatWouldChange": "Quantitative analysis showing that pre-deployment red-teaming requirements correlate with a measurable decline in industry-wide innovation rates.",
